            "paragraph": "These states are followed by Meghalaya (0.5) and Mizoram (0.5) and have a moderate exposure index (Fig. 2). It is mainly because of the high intoxication rate (0.63) and disease load (0.56) in Mizoram; however, variation in rainfall component (0.35) is less, which has lowered the overall exposure. In Meghalaya, moderate exposure is attributed to the highest variation in temperature (0.62) and rainfall (0.61), while the relatively low disease load (0.24) decreases the overall exposure. A 1 \u00b0C increase in summer mean temperature correlated with a 1.0% rise in death rates, with higher temperature variation in both summer and winter proving detrimental, and the excess mortality during hotter summers being solely attributed to temperature anomalies [45].",
