            "target_entity_type": "Country_Subdivision",
            "paragraph": "Vulnerability assessment clearly depicts that Assam is most vulnerable state in the northeastern region (Table 3; Fig. 7), as shown by consistently high scores across multiple vulnerability indices. This is because of its high sensitivity level (0.66) and the least adaptive capacity (0.20) of all the north eastern states. The Diouf vulnerability index records Assam at 1.18, the highest among all states, while the IPCC index also places it at a high vulnerability score of 0.82. This represents Assam's number of issues, which include a vulnerable population, substantial infrastructure gaps in the healthcare system, and high out-of-pocket medical expenses. Even after having a low exposure level (0.36) than states like Arunachal Pradesh and Tripura, its overall adaptive capacity is limited, and it is especially susceptible to the adverse health effects of climate change and its social economic sensitivities. Arunachal Pradesh is classified as low vulnerable",
